{
  "about": [
    "The payloads Prosperous knows about: what each one is, where it is published, and the",
    "digest to check it against once it is downloaded.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE. These entries were read from a target's own payload-manager repository at",
    "/data/pldmgr/repository_cache.json on 2026-08-26, not composed here. That file is one",
    "tool's cache rather than a standard - see docs/DECISIONS.md D016 - and this project",
    "carries a copy so that a fresh install is useful before it has ever seen a target.",
    "",
    "Every entry states a url and a 64-character SHA-256. That is what makes them fetchable:",
    "an entry whose digest cannot be checked is refused BEFORE it is downloaded, so nothing",
    "unverifiable is ever written to disk. The nine-entry list this replaced stated neither,",
    "and so could describe payloads without being able to get any of them.",
    "",
    "THIS LIST IS EDITABLE AND IS MEANT TO BE EDITED. It is written to",
    "~/.config/prosperous/payloads.json on first run and read from there afterwards, so a",
    "correction needs a text editor rather than a rebuild. Reading a target merges its",
    "repository into whatever is there; fields this file has and the target's does not - the",
    "ports below - survive that, because an absence is not a correction.",
    "",
    "Five entries carry a port, and those are the five services this project probes. A port is",
    "what makes presence answerable at all: without one, whether a payload is running is",
    "unknown rather than absent. Add a port to any entry here and the next check measures it.",
    "A WRONG port does not fail loudly - it reports some other listener's state under this",
    "name - so write one you have verified, never one inferred from a description."
  ],
